# Every data source used at request time beyond the two below is a free,
# keyless public API (NYC GeoSearch, NYC Open Data PLUTO/subway snapshots),
# so this app can run with zero environment variables at all if you skip
# durable leads/admin — the JSON stdout log still works either way.

# Durable lead storage + search analytics (db.py). A Neon Postgres instance,
# provisioned through Vercel's Storage tab (Marketplace Database Providers ->
# Neon) so the connection string is injected automatically, never committed.
# For local dev: `vercel env pull .env.local` after connecting the DB.
# DATABASE_URL=

# Shared secret gating GET /admin and /api/admin/* (leads + stats). Pick any
# long random string and set it both here (for local dev) and on Vercel
# (Project -> Settings -> Environment Variables) — never hardcode it.
# ADMIN_API_KEY=

# The frontend's optional Google Maps mode (index.html's GMAPS_KEY constant)
# is a browser-side, HTTP-referrer-restricted key, not a backend secret — it
# stays a hardcoded constant in index.html by design (see the comment above
# it), not an env var, because it's meant to be publicly visible in the
# shipped JS. Restrict it to your domain in Google Cloud Console before
# adding one.
